    "verdict": "alignment_not_discriminative",
    "reason": "the route's score is a count of equal bytes over a 15-byte window: every sentence in this battery is the same eight-word template differing in one two-byte word, so a never-written word and the face's own word at the same position cost exactly the same two bytes.  The eight base records are byte-identical to the template, so any single-word paraphrase is closer to a base record (two mismatched bytes) than to its own record (four), which is why the paraphrases score like the negatives and the write-back alone reaches the maximum."
  },
